<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  The suggestions panel must search the way the SEARCH RESULTS PAGE searches.

  Magento\CatalogSearch\Model\ResourceModel\Fulltext\Collection takes a
  `searchRequestName` and its constructor DEFAULTS it to
  'catalog_view_container' — the category-browse request. Its
  _renderFiltersBefore() then branches on that name, so a keyword query run
  through the default would not be the query the results page runs.

  Core solves this with virtual types in module-catalog-search/etc/di.xml:

      Fulltext\CollectionFactory        -> Collection (catalog_view_container)
      Fulltext\SearchCollectionFactory  -> SearchCollection (quick_search_container)

  ...but SearchCollectionFactory ALONE IS STILL NOT ENOUGH, and picking it was
  a real bug here: the panel reported "6 products" for a term whose results
  page reported 909.

  ===========================================================================
  WHY THE COUNT COLLAPSED TO THE PAGE SIZE
  ===========================================================================
  Fulltext\Collection resolves its total through a TotalRecordsResolver, and
  the DEFAULT one (module-catalog-search) returns null — its own docblock says
  "For Mysql search engine we can't resolve total record count before full
  load of collection". Framework\Data\Collection\AbstractDb::getSize() then
  falls through to a COUNT over the select... which SearchResultApplier has
  already narrowed to `entity_id IN (<this page's ids>)`. So getSize() returns
  the page size. Ask for 6 cards, get told there are 6 products.

  The engine modules replace that resolver. elasticsearchTotalRecordsResolver
  returns $searchResult->getTotalCount() — the engine's real hit count — and
  AbstractDb::getSize() keeps it, because line 437 reads
  `$this->_totalRecords = $this->_totalRecords ?? fetchOne($sql)`: calling
  getSelectCountSql() on the line above runs _renderFiltersBefore(), which is
  where the resolver populates _totalRecords, and the null-coalesce then
  preserves it instead of the COUNT.

  ===========================================================================
  WHAT IS INJECTED, AND WHY THIS EXACT NAME
  ===========================================================================
  elasticsearchFulltextSearchCollectionFactory (defined once, in
  module-elasticsearch) builds elasticsearchFulltextSearchCollection:

      searchRequestName          quick_search_container
      totalRecordsResolverFactory elasticsearchTotalRecordsResolver\Factory

  It is not "the Elasticsearch one" so much as "the quick-search one": both
  Magento_Elasticsearch8 and Magento_OpenSearch point their own engine key at
  this same shared virtual type (see their
  elasticsearchLayerSearchItemCollectionProvider), and MySQL search was
  removed in 2.4 — so on 2.4.8 this is the collection quick search uses under
  every supported engine, and it is the one behind /catalogsearch/result.
  Panel rail, panel count and the "view all" page are now one search.

  ===========================================================================
  WHY WIRED HERE INSTEAD OF TYPE-HINTED
  ===========================================================================
  Every name above is a VIRTUAL TYPE: no class file, so PHP reflection cannot
  resolve it and `setup:di:compile` aborts with "Class ... does not exist".
  SuggestionProvider therefore hints the real base class,
  Catalog\Model\ResourceModel\Product\CollectionFactory — which is what this
  whole virtual-type chain ultimately extends — exactly as core's own
  Layer\Category\ItemCollectionProvider does.
-->
<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:ObjectManager/etc/config.xsd">
    <type name="Spartrak\Search\Model\SuggestionProvider">
        <arguments>
            <argument name="collectionFactory" xsi:type="object">elasticsearchFulltextSearchCollectionFactory</argument>
        </arguments>
    </type>
</config>
